         <title><![CDATA[Aspen Air service gets you between Niagara and Toronto in 11 minutes. It's now 5 days a week]]></title>
         <link>https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/hamilton/aspen-air-niagara-toronto-9.7433059?cmp=rss</link>
         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/6038d3a8-5dab-4dfe-84b0-96d165e6d058,1795469564183/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C186%2C4032%2C2268%29%3B' alt='A city skyline is visible through the window of an aircraft on a runway.' width='620' height='349' title='The Toronto skyline sits over the wing of an Aspen Air aircraft at Billy Bishop Airport. Aspen Air has expanded its 11-minute flights from Niagara to Toronto to five days a week.'/><p>Aspen Air has added two more flight days to its weeks-old route connecting Niagara and Toronto. The airline, based in Kitchener-Waterloo, launched the 11-minute flights from Niagara District Airport airport in Niagara-on-the-Lake to Toronto's Billy Bishop Airport at the beginning of November. Airport and airline executives say strong early demand prompted the company to add Tuesday and Thursday flights.</p>]]></description>
